WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:05.037
Before R can open a file, it needs to know where to look.

2
00:00:05.037 --> 00:00:09.601
In this lesson, you will learn to check your working directory, set a new

3
00:00:09.601 --> 00:00:14.490
one, and calmly fix the error that appears when the path is not quite right.

4
00:00:14.490 --> 00:00:16.120
Let's find our folder together.

5
00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:19.503
We start with getwd.

6
00:00:19.503 --> 00:00:22.509
It shows the folder R is using now:

7
00:00:22.509 --> 00:00:25.140
the R Teaching folder on the desktop.

8
00:00:27.500 --> 00:00:31.093
But our data file is inside the Session Two folder.

9
00:00:31.093 --> 00:00:36.123
So we use setwd, and inside the brackets, in quotes, we write the full

10
00:00:36.123 --> 00:00:37.560
path to that folder.

11
00:00:42.500 --> 00:00:44.527
I type the path carefully:

12
00:00:44.527 --> 00:00:48.580
Users, my user name, Desktop, R Teaching, and Session Two.

13
00:01:02.500 --> 00:01:04.497
Run it, and R says:

14
00:01:04.497 --> 00:01:06.494
Error, cannot change working directory.

15
00:01:06.494 --> 00:01:10.887
That means the path does not match a real folder exactly.

16
00:01:10.887 --> 00:01:15.280
Even one wrong character, or a missing space, will cause this.

17
00:01:29.500 --> 00:01:34.637
Here I open the folder on the computer to check the exact folder name.

18
00:01:34.637 --> 00:01:37.940
The folder is called two, dot, space, Session Two.

19
00:01:42.500 --> 00:01:46.552
I try again with double slashes, and a few small changes.

20
00:01:46.552 --> 00:01:51.340
Each time, I read the message, compare the path, and fix one thing.

21
00:02:07.500 --> 00:02:09.221
And this time it works.

22
00:02:09.221 --> 00:02:11.630
getwd now shows the Session Two folder.

23
00:02:11.630 --> 00:02:15.760
In the Files pane, we can see our data file inside it.

24
00:02:47.500 --> 00:02:50.240
I add clear notes in the script:

25
00:02:50.240 --> 00:02:53.763
understanding the working directory, and setting the working directory.

26
00:02:53.763 --> 00:02:58.460
Notes like these help you, and anyone who reads your script later.

27
00:03:07.500 --> 00:03:07.879
Tip:

28
00:03:07.879 --> 00:03:12.423
if typing the path is hard, RStudio can do it for you.

29
00:03:12.423 --> 00:03:15.452
Use the Session menu, then Set Working Directory.

30
00:03:15.452 --> 00:03:18.860
Next, we will open our Excel file. Well done!

